<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
        <artifactId>qits-projects</artifactId>
        <version>2026.809.145714</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <!-- The git SUBSTRATE: a local mirror per repository, and the pushes that are now the only way
         a ref moves. Nothing about projects, repositories or rows is here — those stay in `domain`,
         which calls this through a handful of records and two declared ports.

         WHY IT IS ITS OWN MODULE. This service used to reach into the bare origins qits-artifacts
         serves, on the shared `qits-repositories` volume, and write refs there directly. That is
         what made skeleton commits, branch creates and deletes, and pulled-in commits fire no
         post-receive and produce no CI run. Removing it means every one of those becomes a push —
         and a push needs somewhere to push FROM, which is the mirror.

         FRAMEWORK-FREE, deliberately, mirroring qits-workspaces' `gitmirror`: no Quarkus, no CDI, no
         MicroProfile config, no Jackson. It takes its collaborators as constructor arguments, so its
         tests run offline against throwaway local bares with no container, no database and no
         augmentation — holding this repo's "a clone of this repo alone builds and tests green" rule
         one module deeper. `domain` owns the one CDI producer that builds it from config.

         NO WORKTREE. Unlike qits-workspaces, which merges and version-bumps in a checkout, this
         service only ever manufactures a commit with plumbing that needs no working tree at all —
         `hash-object`/`update-index`/`write-tree`/`commit-tree` for the project template skeleton,
         and `commit-tree -p -p` on a `merge-tree`-produced tree for a diverged pull. Both move here
         unchanged, which is the whole reason this module is smaller than qits-workspaces' `gitmirror`. -->
    <artifactId>qits-projects-gitmirror</artifactId>
    <name>qits-projects :: gitmirror</name>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <!-- The parent sets java.util.logging.manager=org.jboss.logmanager.LogManager for
                     every module; this one has no jboss-logmanager on its test classpath (no
                     Quarkus here at all), so that override is cleared rather than inherited. -->
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <systemPropertyVariables combine.self="override"/>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
